<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liu Jiyuan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/992">992</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liu Jiyuan was the last ruler of Northern Han, the Shatuo-led state at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiyuan">Taiyuan</a> that was the last of the Ten Kingdoms to resist the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a>, reigning from 968 to 979. Supported by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Khitan Liao</a>, Northern Han withstood Song sieges in 968 and 969. In 979 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-song">Emperor Taizong of Song</a> defeated the Liao relief army and besieged Taiyuan until Liu Jiyuan surrendered, completing the Song reunification.</p></div>
